  "patient": "I I kind of think it has. Well I you know because I have had I've had kind of a lot of loneliness, you know, with my mom being she really didn't like the way I kept my room when I was little, young and she would want me to clean it out and I you know I would fight her and then and then you know the stuffed animal thing was really tough and then she got rid of some of my clothes that were too small for me but I had loved those clothes and some of them she made. I mean there was an alphabet dress. Wow, we called it my alphabet dress and I had my picture taken in it and she got was getting rid of it and I just it was like a relative. I couldn't and then she did it, you know, and so our relationship became so so cold or was always cold. I don't know. And so I think you know I remember in my college roommate I had half the room pretty stacked with clothes and newspapers and papers and she got she just hated it. So I'm trying to think what what would have set it off. It seemed like I do find it somehow comforting. I don't know why exactly but it feels like I'm kind of contained maybe and maybe I don't like empty spaces. I don't feel comfortable in big rooms.",
  "therapist": "Yeah, tell me more about that. What is it?",
